# Tome of the Dead CONCEPT round-2 plastered wall tiles — DRAFT for user review.
# Format = tools/gfx_convert.py --mode tile. Same ink/paper as the existing WALL ($01 in air
# rows). Plaster = solid ink; bare brick = the existing wall pattern (mortar ink, faces paper),
# in register with it (period 4 px across, 8 px down), so a hole/edge continues the global
# brick grid. Brick pixels touching plaster are paper: a 1-px recess shadow at the break.
# Edge contract: plaster/plaster_crack/plaster_hole have all-plaster borders; plaster_edge is
# plaster on top, brick at the bottom, and its left/right borders change at the same row (4),
# so a row of plaster_edge tiles joins plaster above and the existing wall below seamlessly.
# Air rows only: in floor rows walls use $0F, where solid plaster would read as solid white.
=== plaster ink:blue paper:black
########
########
#####.##
########
########
########
#.######
########

=== plaster_crack ink:blue paper:black
###.####
###.####
####.###
####.###
#####.##
####.#.#
######.#
#######.

=== plaster_hole ink:blue paper:black
########
###..###
##..#.##
#...#..#
#.###.##
##...###
###.####
########

=== plaster_edge ink:blue paper:black
########
########
########
####.###
#.#.#.##
........
..#...#.
..#...#.
